<title>COLOMBIA: Colombian stocks close higher.</title>
<headline>Colombian stocks close higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombian stocks rose in Bogota and edged up in Medellin, led by foreign demand for banks, brokers said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Bogota's IBB index climbed 3.66 percent to close at 877.91. Medellin's IBOMED index gained 0.55 percent to close at 13,543.9, in the first session after Monday's Epiphany bank holiday.</p>
<p>&quot;Foreign funds are stepping in to take advantage of the low prices. There's a bit of speculation too that seems to appear when the fixed term bond market is slow,&quot; one Bogota broker said.</p>
</text>
